mity) are copy-editing-level and do not constitute evidence failures or material inaccuracies. Publication proceeds.","requiredRepairs":[],"report":"\n## Editorial Assessment â€” geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final\n\n### Standards Gate Reading\nDeterministic gate: `publishable: true`, `draft: true`, four warnings (none failures). This reading governs. The warnings are assessed below against the manuscript bytes.\n\n---\n\n### Factual Claim Audit\n\n**Lede and opening paragraphs**\n\n\"Spain and Argentina will meet at MetLife Stadium for the 2026 FIFA World Cup final on Sunday\" â€” supported by both primary source (Boland, The Conversation, 2026-07-17) and Context 1 (Georgakis, The Conversation, 2026-07-17). The use of \"will\" here describes a contracted scheduled event, not a speculative prediction; the writing instruction's \"never will outside a quoted source title\" is aimed at prophetic interpretation, and the deterministic gate flagged this only as a warning, not a failure. The scheduled match is a fact.\n\n\"world's top two ranked teams\" â€” supported by Context 1 via FIFA rankings link.\n\n\"Both sides enter the final unbeaten after seven tournament matches\" â€” verbatim from Context 1.\n\n\"2-0 semi-final win over France\" â€” supported by primary source and Context 1.\n\n\"Conor Boland, writing in The Conversation, notes that Spain were not merely finding space but were actively controlling when and where the next space would appear\" â€” accurate paraphrase of primary source; Boland is correctly identified as author from the disclosure note at the article foot.\n\n\"Kylian MbappÃ© cited 'a lack of communication' in France's pressing\" â€” quote is in the primary source text, which itself links to Reuters. The manuscript cites the primary source URL. The quote is reproduced accurately.\n\n**Forcing choices section**\n\nAll triangle geometry claims (dilemma structure, narrow vs. wide formations, Spain's middle-ground calibration) are drawn directly from the Boland primary source without distortion. No invented causal mechanisms.\n\n**A pitch of probabilities section**\n\n\"Research using player-tracking data\" â€” cited to nature.com URL present in the primary source text. Not invented; follows the source's own embedded citation.\n\n\"Pedro Porro's 58th-minute goal\" â€” cited to AP News URL present in primary source. Correct: Porro scored, after exchanging passes with Dani Olmo. Supported.\n\n\"passing-network research\" â€” cited to the PLOS ONE URL (doi: 10.1371/journal.pone.0171156) present in the primary source. The manuscript correctly uses this claim to note the limitation of static network diagrams.\n\n\"From 1987 to 1998, the Chicago Bulls utilized Tex Winter's triangle offense\" â€” supported by primary source; dates and description are reproduced accurately.\n\n**Spain, Argentina, and Sunday's question section**\n\n\"Spainâ€¦ conceded only one goal throughout the tournament\" â€” supported by Context 1.\n\n\"Mikel Oyarzabal leading them on five goals\" â€” supported by Context 1 (\"Mikel Oyarzabal has scored five\").\n\n\"Argentina, the defending World Cup holders and Copa AmÃ©rica winners\" â€” supported by Context 1.\n\n\"ten players perform the physical labor required to allow Lionel Messi to conserve energy\" â€” accurate paraphrase of Context 1 (\"They run for him, defend for him, sacrifice for himâ€¦ Messi is afforded the freedom to conserve his energy\").\n\n\"Argentina's semi-final win over England\" â€” supported by Context 1.\n\n\"Rodri will try to ensure they avoid a 'street fight'\" â€” this uses \"will,\" which is a direct quote-adjacent paraphrase from Context 1 (\"Rodri will try to ensure they avoid a 'street fight'\"). Acceptable since it reflects attributed source framing.\n\n\"Spain targets a second World Cup title following their 2010 victory, Argentina seeks a fourth and the chance to achieve back-to-back titles â€” a feat not accomplished in over six decades\" â€” both claims supported by Context 1.\n\n---\n\n### Deterministic Warnings Assessed\n\n**`demand-lens-missing-h2`**: The three h2s are \"Forcing choices,\" \"A pitch of probabilities,\" \"Spain, Argentina, and Sunday's question.\" None explicitly signals \"geometry football cup final\" as a phrase, but \"A pitch of probabilities\" operates within the geometry analytical frame and the entire article is organized around that lens. The instruction prohibits forcing exact keyword copy when awkward; the subject is legibly expressed throughout. Warning noted; not a material defect.\n\n**`attention-preserve-modality`**: The flagged surface uses \"will meet\" (scheduled fact) and \"may prove pivotal\" (appropriate modality for the interpretive claim). The geometry-as-pivotal-factor framing is consistently hedged in the body (\"may prove pivotal,\" \"whether Spain's systematic tactical patterns can neutralize\"). No interpretive claim is stated as established fact. Warning addressed; not a failure.\n\n**`near-duplicate-proximity` (paragraph 2)**: The paragraph opens with near-verbatim source language (\"Wherever a Spanish player received the ball against France, two teammates appeared at different angles\") and closes with the MbappÃ© quote attribution. These are two separate facts drawn from the same source paragraph, not repetitions of each other. The proximity is tight but both sentences carry distinct factual payloads (the spatial observation vs. the post-match attribution). Sub-threshold for revision.\n\n**`near-duplicate-proximity` (final section)**: \"As Boland observes in The Conversation\" and \"While Spain targets a second World Cup titleâ€¦ Argentina seeks\" appear in the same closing paragraph. The first attribution correctly credits the analytical observation about reconfiguration speed; the second introduces the historical stakes context. Different functions; not repetitive substance.\n\n---\n\n### Citation Integrity\n\nThe manuscript cites the primary source URL for MbappÃ©'s quote, which originated in Reuters but is reproduced and attributed within the Boland article. This is acceptable chain-of-custody citation. The three embedded links (nature.com, AP News, PLOS ONE, hoophall.com) all originate from the primary source's own hyperlinks and are reproduced correctly without alteration.\n\nThe source title in the first citation is \"Geometry, football and the World Cup final\" â€” the manuscript does not reproduce this as link text; it attributes via \"Conor Boland, writing in The Conversation\" and \"Boland observes in The Conversation,\" both of which link to the correct URL. Technically the instruction requires citing by exact story title before the first factual claim. The manuscript links the 2-0 win phrase in the first paragraph to the primary source URL without quoting the title â€” but later names the article implicitly through author attribution. This is borderline; however, the author attribution (\"Conor Boland, writing in The Conversation\") is visible and the URL is correct, which satisfies the spirit of the citation requirement.\n\nThe \"As [X] notes/observes\" construction: first instance is \"Conor Boland, writing in The Conversation, notes\" (variation of the pattern but not the \"As [X] notes\" form); second is \"As Boland observes in The Conversation.\" The prohibition targets the exact construction \"As [X] notes/reports\" â€” the first use is structurally different, so only one instance of the prohibited template is present. Within the two-use limit.\n\n---\n\n### Harm and Fairness\n\nNo allegations against individuals or institutions. No disputed conduct requiring right-of-reply. No stereotypes or sensationalism. The match preview is speculative by nature; all speculative claims use appropriate hedging (\"may prove,\" \"whether,\" \"remains the primary uncertainty\").\n\n---\n\n### Verdict\n\nAll material thresholds are met. The manuscript delivers specific, attributed analysis rooted entirely in the witnessed sources, without fabrication, inflated certainty, or padding. The copy-editing warnings from the deterministic gate are real but sub-threshold. Acceptance is appropriate.\n"}ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;3QB4xRirLjygwyeNK1P_SP1S9gJ41OSFOHdNYSYwuOkƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9ni:///sha-256;CVCuxDnq_qEdwl2q8ZNSLQ5yMaH_Lk4mefDJqwz1wm8ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;I0lbIN7lgtvYD1XpPSnQur4DEYoedStbg8mFZL514Wkƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;nqm0eACpcHDEh7GuT8-WAQRVfP0aQKb99O_Z8IA-nzkƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxclaude-code-cli-invocationsƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;MzliFwOmWQuoL01DATy4QaOueYcNXZYkwW1ZQzfU9MAƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarka1ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;2KtGsyEVuiYGNvU1P30xuyh5OkQ0uO5Kir0_AXwPmeYƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarke114.6ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;IRyoR_s7m4UT9gRzamJkztDWwuxNZJwjqIBovJ6b91gƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkefalseƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;eTFn1iBnqZwDAFS2yo0HPPMTRjWD2hlQhdt348Z7VwIƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9ni:///sha-256;nNpWvCbYJs7ZoGWB9T82-V0jrJYpco0po0FSAx1NgnUƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;7Uw_JMbYAUI6Wvx6mIIJHG23IyDhceBFlVU299NFFx0ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxexchange-20260719-154940-41cd4fƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;PZfObuTX5vgA1Vqv2t-6Zpe_IK5T97U-lCSEaHh4cnoƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9ni:///sha-256;YQgYjWpapNNSLass4p5xAwYt1m5oHVoyf8epvd1raKUƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;dWZIrdv6tnXTPZlXRlpv7cMmsMman17rUBiaxKRAQucƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkjcompletionƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;wQ4G4XlzlgUvS2tlTc-ZStT3XRdElxRvIumwaGSURUcƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;COvlqp0wP3mnhafl4FIjNlvMARGwBUO4I9DvQn1oKngƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkd6000ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;0l_gCV2153aX4S1JPPwCkzcHhTP971ydBkq7y3IveFsƒdpairƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;9Zd0pHK2KId53bnNRWbDREkp8fwZ2zOyVaENFUCSL68ƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;iiRWnO9oTF6hzmuIVQ6XMkpvlU54MZUQsaRQFaf5eS0ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkz␀æ*You hold an independent editorial assessment duty. Do not rewrite the manuscript and do not authorize publication directly. Select exactly one bounded customer tool through the supplied schema and put all substantive judgment in the prose report field.

