{"slug":"geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final","publishable":true,"draft":true,"wordCount":701,"referenceCount":2,"seoTerm":"geometry football cup final","findings":[{"severity":"warning","gate":"standards-cleared","code":"demand-lens-missing-h2","message":"A level-two heading should naturally signal the demand lens when the reporting supports it; exact keyword copy is not required."},{"severity":"warning","gate":"standards-cleared","code":"attention-preserve-modality","message":"surface \"Spain's Geometry Meets Messi's Magic in World Cup Final Showdown. Spain and Argentina will meet at MetLife Stadium for the 2026 FIFA World Cup final on Sunday, a clash between the worldâ€™s top two ranked teams. Both sides enter the final unbeaten after seven tournament matches. In their 2-0 semi-final win over France, Spainâ€™s performance was anchored by passing trianglesâ€”a tactical framework that may prove pivotal against Argentina.\" uses certainty language for interprets warrant"},{"severity":"warning","gate":"copy-edited","code":"near-duplicate-proximity","message":"Two sentences in one paragraph repeat multiple short phrases: Wherever a Spanish player received the ball against France, two teammates appeared at diff / Following the match, Kylian MbappÃ© cited [\"a lack of communication\" in France's pressing]("},{"severity":"warning","gate":"copy-edited","code":"near-duplicate-proximity","message":"Two sentences in one paragraph repeat multiple short phrases: As [Boland observes in The Conversation](https://theconversation.com/geometry-football-and / While Spain targets a second World Cup title following their 2010 victory, Argentina seeks"}],"kind":"producing-content.standards-review"}

